  "spiritual_reading": "\n\n\n#\n Spiritual\n Translation\n\n\n**\n¶1:**\n Wisdom,\n in\n the very\n origin\n of all\n things, existed\n in full\nness. The Divine\n Word\n,\n which\n is the first\n proce\neding of all\n understanding\n, concerned\n itself\n with the separation of what\n is true\n from what is false.\n The most\n elevated states\n of the\n mind\n were raised\n toward\n still\n higher states of\n perception\n, and these\n expanded\n until the\n conflict\n between good\n and evil should\n begin\n.\n The domin\nion of wisdom\n existed\n in those\n elevated\n states, proce\neding from all\n the successive\n un\nfoldings of spiritual\n life —\n that\n wisdom\n which\n no\n fals\nity has\n ever entered\n.\n\n\n**¶2:**\n Falsity and evil,\n which\n constitute\n the unre\ngen\nerate mind, had\n their\n origin\n deep\n within\n the natural will\n. They\n p\noured forth from themselves\n ce\naselessly.\n All\n that\n the\n merely\n natural man\n poss\nesses belongs\n to this\n realm\n of spiritual\n darkness\n. It\n is utt\nerly remote\n from wisdom\n.\n\n**¶3:** This\n is the first teaching\n concerning the eternal\n states:\n that good\n and evil each\n exist in their own nature;\n that they\n are divided from one another by\n their very essence\n,\n and\n have\n been\n so from\n et\nernity. Yet\n fals\nity and evil rose\n up against wisdom and good, des\niring to reign over a\n spiritual\n substance\n that did\n not belong to them. Evil\n spread\n cont\nention into\n what\n was\n peaceful\n;\n it disturbed the order\n of\n spiritual life\n, and asc\nended against\n it\n —\n and\n in this arose\n the great\n spiritual\n crisis\n.\n\n**¶4:** The\n Divine\n Power\n went\n forth from the\n Infinite\n —\n which is the Divine\n Human in\n His\n first\n proce\neding.\n He cloth\ned Himself in divine\n truths as in\n an\n armor of\n wisdom\n,\n and went\n to meet\n all\n the \nenmity\n of\n evil. He subd\nued and\n fixed it upon\n its\n own nature\n,\n so\n that its\n power\n of\n agg\nression was\n arrested\n by\n those\n very\n truths it\n had sought\n to destroy\n.\n\n\n**¶5:** He\n brought forth\n divine\n love as\n the ruling\n good\n of\n the spiritual\n world\n, and all\n the un\nfol\ndings of wisdom\n were\n illumin\nated by it\n. The\n Divine proce\neding as\n ordering Providence\n established\n the whole\n spiritual\n universe\n. The natural\n mind was\n set in place\n.\n Wisdom\n and\n fals\nity,\n which from\n the beginning existed\n in their\n own n\natures, were now\n distinguished\n and arranged\n,\n and the external\n truths by\n which the\n mind\n is\n cloth\ned were given\n to each\n degree\n.\n He\n ordered\n the successive\n states of spiritual progression\n —\n the\n recurring\n cycles by\n which the inter\niors\n of the mind\n are opened\n —\n and these\n were set in the\n highest\n places,\n so that they\n might govern\n all\n that\n is of\n fals\nity and\n evil.\n The\n foundation\n of divine\n order\n was made\n firm,\n and every\n part of the arrangement\n was established.\n\n**¶6\n:** Beneath\n the\n celest\nial degree\n he\n set\n all\n lower\n things\n;\n and above the\n natural\n mind he established\n three degrees\n of external\n reception\n,\n con\njoined\n one\n to\n another. He enclosed the natural\n mind\n within\n four\n elevated\n states\n of\n perception and\n three\n containing\n forms of\n truth,\n together\n with its\n general\n knowledges and\n its\n higher\n app\nrehensions —\n all set\n in order upon it. This whole\n spiritual\n arrangement\n stood\n firm as a restra\nint upon the powers of evil, binding\n them —\n for\n the\n good that\n had\n become\n ent\nangled with fals\nity was\n now held\n within\n a\n structure\n capable\n of separ\nating them\n.\n\n**¶7:** Then\n came\n the Divine\n proce\neding in\n its\n third manner — as\n Re\ndeemer.\n It\n purified all\n wisdom\n that\n had been obsc\nured,\n by\n presenting\n the\n image\n of the Divine Human itself\n.\n It became the means\n of redem\nption for all things.\n\n**\n¶8:** All\n states\n of good\n and evil exist\n throughout\n the whole\n spiritual\n constitution\n of\n the human\n being\n.\n The\n fire of\n self-love blaz\nes within the\n natural mind, and it dev\nours what\n surro\nunds it. But\n whatever\n is of\n genuine\n wisdom\n is\n also\n present\n there\n:\n it\n becomes\n the\n purifying\n agent, and when\n freed\n,\n it\n asc\nends to the\n spiritual\n degree\n that\n is\n its true\n home\n.\n Conversely, whatever\n is of falsity and evil is drawn\n out\n and gathered together\n into a bond of\n con\nfinement.\n The inter\niors\n are\n unveiled\n;\n all\n things\n of\n good\n enter\n into the Divine and\n become\n one with it —\n they\n become\n as\n the\n frag\nrance of worship\n —\n and the\n whole\n is\n established\n.\n Good\n and truth\n reign\n forever, and the\n one\n Divine\n comes to be known\n as sole\n sovereign\n over the\n whole of\n the\n mind\n,\n above\n every\n state\n within\n it.\n From\n that\n time on\nward there\n is found\n no advers\nary against the Father, who\n is the sovereign\n of all wisdom\n and all\n good\n.\n\n**¶9:** These\n are\n the states in\n which all\n spiritual\n things\n unf\nold,\n from the very\n beginning:\n good\n and evil,\n truth and falsity, are\n inter\nmingled and con\njoined with\n one another —\n and\n the\n entire\n work\n of regener\nation is their\n separation\n.",
  "reconstructions": [
    {
      "paragraph": 1,
      "reconstructed_text": "(1) [The teaching of the] Light [is that] which he has unveiled [to (2) all of] his disciples [. The (3)] entire [mystery] of wisdom [and every] word in the beginning [he proclaimed] concerning the separation [of the Light from the Darkness. The aeons rose in] the heights [and ascended] to the heights [of the Light,] and they spread out [in their fullness. Then the Darkness rose up unt]il they should make war [against the] kingdom [of the L]ight [that abides] in the heights [f]rom all the aeons [of] the Light, the one that no [Darkness has ever entered] in it."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 2,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Below exists] the Darkness, the world [of evil, and] their root [is in the depth,] which poured forth [from itself ceaselessly.] the one that the earth has [brought forth from itself is of the] Darkness [entirely, and] it is far from the Light [of the heights.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 3,
      "reconstructed_text": "for each one of them exists [in its own nature, and] they are divided from one another by their [essence and their being] in an eternality since the [beginning of time.] (4) the Darkness has made war against the Light, desiring that it would reign over an essence not its own. It spread a quarrel [into the place of peace, and] it disturbed [the order of the Light. It] came up, it [set itself against the Light. And in this great] need."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 4,
      "reconstructed_text": "The power came forth from [the Father of Greatness, which] is [the Fir]st Man. He [clothed himself in] the armour of Light [and went forth against] all [the enmity]. He crucified it in [the depth of matter, and] the armour [of Light bound its power.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 5,
      "reconstructed_text": "[Then] he brought the sun [and the moon to illuminate] the Light aeons [in the heights. And the] Living Spirit spread out the universe [and established] the earth [beneath. He separated] the Light and the Darkness in the beginning [of the creation,] and the garments. He gave [them to every degree of the powers.] He set in order the [heavens and the firmaments] and the wheel of the course [of the stars] in the heights, that they would [govern every power] of the Darkness. He stood firm [and was f]ixed. He constructed the foundation [of the whole, and] all of it was set up."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 6,
      "reconstructed_text": "Underneath [the firmaments he placed] all of them; and also above he [set in place the thre]e earths, they being conjoined. He enclosed the earth in [the midst of f]our mountains and three vessels [, together with all that is] in its seas and its mountains [, all set in] order upon it. This universe stood firm [as] a bond for the evil powers [, restraining the li]ght that they joined with the Darkness [within this structure.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 7,
      "reconstructed_text": "Then the Third Ambassador! [He purified the Light] by his image. He became [redeemer of] all things."
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 8,
      "reconstructed_text": "(5) [The powers of good and evil,] they are in all the [parts of the u]niverse, and the fire blazes in it, and it is devoured [by the fire. But] all [the substance] of the Light also, and he becomes purifier, and goes up to his essence. Conversely, the Darkness which is in [it is drawn] out, and it is gathered in to a bond [of confinement. The hidden things] unveil [themselves,] and they go in to him and become [as a sweet pe]rfume [. The whole is s]et up [in truth, an]d they reign for ever, and a single God comes to be [sovereign ov]er the totality, being above the totality. You find no opponent from this time on against the Father, the King of the Light and the [Lord of all wisdom and goodness.]"
    },
    {
      "paragraph": 9,
      "reconstructed_text": "[These are the states in] which they occur in, from the beginning [of all things until their final separation:] they are mixed and joined with one another."
    }
  ],
